# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# The game used to be one HTML file, and this file still said so long after it
# was split into css/ and js/. Only the HTML had a cache rule, so browsers kept
# serving stale stylesheets and scripts after a deploy: new markup, old layout,
# and a site that looked unchanged no matter what was uploaded.
#
# Two defences now. These headers stop assets being held indefinitely, and the
# asset URLs in index.html carry a ?v= build tag so an already-cached copy
# cannot be reused at all. Bump the tag in index.html on every release.
# ⚠️  SEARCH ENGINES AND THE MOVE TO thexigames.com/crossword/
#
# This game lives at crossword.thexigames.com and is moving to a path on the
# hub. Until it does, this address is staging: indexing it now would put the
# wrong URL in every result and every link, and a migration that starts from
# somebody else's index of your old address is a much harder migration.
#
# THE RULE, for every game in the family:
#   on a subdomain  ->  X-Robots-Tag: noindex must be here
#   on its path     ->  it must NOT be
#
# deploy_check enforces it. Remove the header in the same commit that moves the
# game, not before and not after.

/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

# no-store, not max-age=0. Both are meant to force a check with the server, but
# must-revalidate leaves room for a browser to serve its copy in edge cases —
# session restore, back/forward, an offline moment — and a stale index.html
# pins a player to an old build permanently, because the versioned asset URLs
# it names are the old ones too. The file is 15KB; fetching it every time costs
# nothing next to shipping someone last week's game.
/
  Cache-Control: no-store

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-store

# Stylesheet and scripts. Versioned in the HTML, so a long cache would be safe,
# but revalidating costs one conditional request and removes a whole class of
# "why has nothing changed" problem.
/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Puzzle responses carry today's clues and must never sit in a shared cache.
# The Functions set this themselves too; this is belt and braces.
/api/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
